            "errorPath": "Report k instead of the area."
          },
          {
            "id": "D",
            "latex": "\\frac{27}{5}",
            "errorPath": "Report the y-coordinate of A."
          },
          {
            "id": "E",
            "latex": "\\frac{2}{5}",
            "errorPath": "Report the vertical separation of A and B."
          },
          {
            "id": "F",
            "latex": "\\frac{4}{5}",
            "errorPath": "Report the horizontal separation of A and B."
          }
        ],
        "correctOptionId": "A",
        "correctAnswerLatex": "\\frac{13}{5}",
        "workedSolutionSteps": [
          "Since the given line has gradient 2, its perpendicular has finite gradient −1/2. Thus A and B cannot have equal x-coordinates (k≠3). The line through B is y=−x/2+13/2. Equate y=2k+1 at x=k to get k=11/5 and A=(11/5,27/5).",
          "At x=11/5 the line OB, whose equation is y=5x/3, has height 11/3. The vertical separation from A is 27/5−11/3=26/15.",
          "Split triangle OAB at this vertical segment: its two triangle areas add to half the segment length times the total horizontal width 3. Thus area=(26/15)×3/2=13/5."
        ],
