        "topicId": "math-y9-straight-line-graphs",
        "provisionalConceptFamily": "axis-distance-ratio",
        "stem": "A line segment joins (0,6) to (8,0). Points P and Q on the segment have positive coordinates. At P, the distance from the y-axis is twice the distance from the x-axis. At Q, the distance from the x-axis is twice the distance from the y-axis. Find the ratio $PQ:AB$, where A=(0,6), B=(8,0).",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "A",
            "latex": "3:5",
            "errorPath": "Use AP:AB instead of PQ:AB."
          },
          {
            "id": "B",
